                                        "sense_id": "3f17e7cf-125c-3675-819a-d07f3cb2d229",
                                        "entry_id": "18c3a626-3de9-3a31-89d9-522fa70aeb46",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The Sun, the star orbited by the Earth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "poetic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2e861938-15d4-3e8f-9388-b0ecd013994b",
                                        "entry_id": "18c3a626-3de9-3a31-89d9-522fa70aeb46",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The sun god; equivalent of the Greek Helios. Brother of Luna and Aurora."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Roman"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd03641b-5b4d-3413-a62c-68cca7aeaab0",
                                        "entry_id": "18c3a626-3de9-3a31-89d9-522fa70aeb46",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The sun goddess."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Norse"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e6cbec0-c100-35b8-83c5-391301e87054",
                                        "entry_id": "18c3a626-3de9-3a31-89d9-522fa70aeb46",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male given name"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "nonce-word"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d41f87c7-a25f-43c4-9980-4f7cb0d5f1e5",
                                                "sense_id": "9e6cbec0-c100-35b8-83c5-391301e87054",
                                                "text": "Sol (named after the solar eclipse on the day of his birth) was born in March 2015 with an undetected clot in his upper left arm."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Sol",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc4b0863-5820-32fc-8b83-a7e609a1a003",
                                        "entry_id": "fc4d51d3-eed2-3ee3-9405-2e0102daca51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Or (gold), in the postmedieval practice of blazoning the tinctures of certain sovereigns' (especially British monarchs') coats as planets."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef79bea2-5f5a-4023-bc51-499b063ee0d4",
                                                "sense_id": "dc4b0863-5820-32fc-8b83-a7e609a1a003",
                                                "text": "4. Luna, a Mantle of Estate, Mars doubled Ermine, ouched Sol, garnished with Strings fastned thereunto fretways dependent, and tasselled of the same. [...] These Arms do belong to the Town of Beckbock in Wales. 5. Jupiter, a Mace of Majestry in Bend Sol."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e08dbc20-e65e-403d-86c6-6918fb98f77e",
                                                "sense_id": "dc4b0863-5820-32fc-8b83-a7e609a1a003",
                                                "text": "George [...] Ist. Mars, three Lions passant guardant in Pale Sol, for the Arms of England, Impal'd with Scotland, i.e. Sol, a Lion rampant within a double Tressure counterflory Mars. 2d. Jupiter, three Fleurs de Lis Sol, for the Arms of France. 3d. Jupiter, an Irish Harp Sol, stringed Luna, for Ireland. 4th. Seme party per Pale, and per Chevron enarche, in the Ist Mars, two Lions passant guardant Sol, for Brunswick. In the 2d Partition Sol, semy of Hearts Mars, and a Lion rampant Jupiter, armed and langued of the First, for Luneburg."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efcb7112-87e7-4489-b98b-b3cecb0bf63b",
                                                "sense_id": "dc4b0863-5820-32fc-8b83-a7e609a1a003",
                                                "text": "8. Tierce in Mantle, first Mars, two Lions passant-guardant in pale, Sol, for Brunswick; 2d Sol, Semi of Hearts proper, a Lion rampant Jupiter, for Lunenburgh;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46027b84-1a80-4b3f-8e70-aad15a2d3e69",
                                                "sense_id": "dc4b0863-5820-32fc-8b83-a7e609a1a003",
                                                "text": "ARMS. QUARTERLY, in the first grand Quarter Mars, three Lions passant-guardant in Pale, Sol; the Imperial Ensigns of England, impaled with the Royal Arms of Scotland, which are Sol, a Lion rampant within a double Tressure flower'd and counterflower'd with Fleurs-de-lis, Mars. The second Quarter is the Royal Arms of France, viz. Jupiter, three Fleurs-de-lis, Sol. The third, the Ensign of Ireland, which is, Jupiter, an Harp Sol, stringed Luna."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0f804925-66e6-32af-bae3-ce4b82580a1b",
                                        "entry_id": "fc4d51d3-eed2-3ee3-9405-2e0102daca51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Gold."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Sol",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d98811ea-6b83-3366-951e-d1a3d85a298c",
                                        "entry_id": "d8e78dcc-7438-32fa-ae00-8cec113c588e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A diminutive of the male given name Solomon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0664e220-377d-4594-b397-64fe85455204",
                                                "sense_id": "d98811ea-6b83-3366-951e-d1a3d85a298c",
                                                "text": "“Chock full o’ science,” said the radiant Captain, “as ever he was! Sol Gills, Sol Gills, what have you been up to, for this many a long day, my ould boy?”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
